    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** anchoring the lineup, carrying an elite score of 83.29. Facing Randy V\u00e1squez, who struggles with a 4.89 xERA, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive 19% boost in SP skill valuation and significant park factors, making him our primary engine for power and counting stats. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (72.20) are high-priority starts today. **Jackson Merrill** is positioned to exploit the weak matchup against Trey Gibson, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** remains a focal point due to his favorable dynamic platoon advantage against Luis Castillo. We are also looking for **Kyle Tucker** (67.23) to provide reliable production; despite a modest base, his consistent efficiency keeps him safely in the optimal starting slots.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Nasim Nunez**, who recorded a score of 53.59. While **Nasim Nunez** offers elite stolen base potential\u2014a core priority for our roster\u2014he was squeezed out by the sheer volume of high-scoring, multi-category contributors currently in the starting nine. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (53.07) came close to cracking the utility spot, but the optimizer prioritized the positional flexibility and platoon advantages offered by **Josh Jung** and **Jacob Wilson**. The biggest risk remains **Sam Antonacci** (45.30), who faces a daunting matchup against the elite arm of Yoshinobu Yamamoto; while his xwOBA of 0.374 keeps his floor intact, the significant negative SP skill adjustment suggests he is a candidate for early substitution if the game script turns sour. With all lineups currently pending, managers must keep a close watch on official batting orders, as any drop in order position for **Liam Hicks** or **Curtis Mead** could dampen their projected efficiency.",
